tnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/24/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/d3e08e91b65a46fc6d88bbb8ba641b6047172ce5/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates float error (`19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `1998`). Fix: round half-up via `Decimal`, matching the half-up convention in `discounts.py`/`tax.py`.\npytest isn't installed, so I'll call the test functions directly.\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, not `totals.py`: `to_cents` did `int(amount * 100)`, and `int()` cuts off the fractional part. Floats can't store prices like 19.99 exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.999\u2026` and became `1998` instead of `1999`. The same thing happened with `0.29` (gave 28) and `4.35` (gave 434).\n\n`to_cents` now converts through `Decimal(str(amount))` and rounds half up, the same rounding rule `discounts.py` and `tax.py` already use.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`. All four tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the one in `tests/test_report.py` pass.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 61628, "requests_cache_write": 16359, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1322566, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests